From 7774c0de3bf024f29de3af17036e134344151baf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:55:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a stalled replica's missing-parent deferral
 is said once per stale stamp at INFO

Review nit on #1931 (5887627668): when the synced replica never reaches the feed head again, children whose
parent status is unknown waited silently, with only a DEBUG line. The readiness pass now counts its deferrals
and logs one INFO line per board per replica stamp (kanban_replica_freshness.report_deferred), naming the board,
the replica's last time at the head (or "no readable replica") and how many children wait; it repeats only when
the replica's pulled_at changes.

kanban_db.recompute_ready now calls kanban_db_graph.note_missing_parents directly (the one-caller
_note_missing_parents facade is gone) so the pass-end report fits kanban_db.py's FILE_LINES cap.

No wall-clock escalation in the detector: after a laptop sleeps for hours its stamp is hours old on wake, so a
bound would fire at once and bring back the false blocks this gate removes. A replica that never catches up is
alarmed in awake time by the sync-freshness check of t_01a1d3df5e5d0757 (one card per incident).

Test: test_a_stalled_replica_is_reported_once_per_stale_stamp_at_info (RED at 7b0bcbb5e2: no INFO line).
